<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexander Karl, Duke of Anhalt-Bernburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1805–1863</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Alexander Charles of Anhalt-Bernburg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexander Karl was the last Duke of Anhalt-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernburg">Bernburg</a>, ruling from 1834 until his death. Because of his mental illness the duchy was largely governed by his ministers and by his wife, Duchess Friederike. He died without children in 1863, and his lands passed to Leopold IV of Anhalt-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dessau">Dessau</a>, who thereby united all the Anhalt territories into a single Duchy of Anhalt.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexander-karl-duke-of-anhalt-bernburg.jpg" alt="Alexander Karl, Duke of Anhalt-Bernburg" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wilhelm von Kügelgen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alexander_Karl,_Duke_of_Anhalt-Bernburg_(1805-1863).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
